WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:05.045
- Yeah.

00:00:05.045 --> 00:00:08.295
(fast-paced pop music)

00:00:09.622 --> 00:00:11.445
- This week we threw it
all the way back to the 90s

00:00:11.445 --> 00:00:13.001
and played with Tamagotchis.

00:00:13.001 --> 00:00:14.939
- I honestly don't know how long I've had

00:00:14.939 --> 00:00:16.843
my original Tamagotchi.

00:00:16.843 --> 00:00:18.506
I actually was a Tamagotchi hoarder.

00:00:18.506 --> 00:00:20.926
- I think I had a Neopet or a Giga Pet,

00:00:20.926 --> 00:00:22.721
'cause it was free in a
Happy Meal or something.

00:00:22.721 --> 00:00:25.180
- I had just lost a tooth and decided

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.240
that night that I was gonna write a letter

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.572
to the Tooth Fairy saying
that instead of a quarter,

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:31.689
I think it'd be really cool if she

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:33.065
brought me a Tamagotchi.

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.561
- Me and my brother got
them because my mom told us

00:00:35.561 --> 00:00:37.976
that we had to keep our Tamagotchis alive

00:00:37.976 --> 00:00:39.381
in order to get a dog.

00:00:39.381 --> 00:00:40.554
We both killed our Tamagotchis

00:00:40.554 --> 00:00:42.341
but we still ended up getting a dog,

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:44.292
so I don't know how that
lesson really worked out.

00:00:44.292 --> 00:00:45.813
- This little guy just
showed up on my desk,

00:00:45.813 --> 00:00:47.253
and without any instructions.

00:00:47.253 --> 00:00:48.588
- I'm so excited to rip this open

00:00:48.588 --> 00:00:49.830
and start taking care of it.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.293
I really hope I don't kill it.

00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:52.918
- The new version is super duper small,

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:55.844
so I'm excited to see how it's gonna be.

00:00:55.844 --> 00:00:57.464
Oh my gosh!

00:00:57.464 --> 00:00:59.510
It is so little.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:01.216
I'm gonna pull this tab right now,

00:01:01.216 --> 00:01:02.795
which is like the best feeling ever,

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:03.654
and bring him to life.

00:01:03.654 --> 00:01:05.349
(beeping)
Ah!

00:01:05.349 --> 00:01:07.387
- Juggling this and work

00:01:07.387 --> 00:01:08.722
is a little tough.

00:01:08.722 --> 00:01:10.521
I have to find a babysitter
when I'm going to

00:01:10.521 --> 00:01:11.903
a really important meeting,

00:01:11.903 --> 00:01:14.353
because I don't want it to
go off when I'm on a call.

00:01:14.353 --> 00:01:17.476
Auntie Liz is taking
care of my Tamagotchi.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.510
- I think I'm feeding him.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:21.117
- Apparently, my Tamagotchi was beeping

00:01:21.117 --> 00:01:22.615
and I had my headphones on at work,

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.950
so Tanner yelled at me.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:24.856
- Yeah.

00:01:24.856 --> 00:01:26.911
It was crying and she was ignoring it.

00:01:26.911 --> 00:01:28.533
She's a bad Tamagotchi mom.

00:01:28.533 --> 00:01:31.331
- Tanner, are you my temp
dad for the Tamagotchi?

00:01:31.331 --> 00:01:34.373
- Me and Gotchi, is what I
call my Tamagotchi for short,

00:01:34.373 --> 00:01:36.915
had truly one of the best
weekends of our lives.

00:01:36.915 --> 00:01:38.796
We went out in the East Village.

00:01:38.796 --> 00:01:40.503
We walked the Brooklyn Bridge.

00:01:40.503 --> 00:01:41.989
We went to the Giants game.

00:01:41.989 --> 00:01:44.764
We shared the most
beautiful New York weekend.

00:01:44.764 --> 00:01:47.272
- I feel like I've had
supernatural experiences

00:01:47.272 --> 00:01:48.723
with my Tamagotchis,

00:01:48.723 --> 00:01:50.813
and this one wasn't an exception.

00:01:50.813 --> 00:01:52.931
I'm honestly kind of tired
of taking care of him

00:01:52.931 --> 00:01:55.102
'cause there's nothing that
exciting that's happening.

00:01:55.102 --> 00:01:57.771
(beeping)

00:01:57.771 --> 00:01:58.604
Oh my God!

00:01:58.604 --> 00:01:59.699
He totally heard me!

00:01:59.699 --> 00:02:00.651
Did you see that?

00:02:00.651 --> 00:02:01.826
This Tamagotchi is just like,

00:02:01.826 --> 00:02:02.987
he listens.

00:02:02.987 --> 00:02:04.357
He's in there. (laughs)

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.083
(beeping)

00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:07.081
You see?

00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:08.208
It's like, it knows.

00:02:08.208 --> 00:02:09.334
Every time I call him boring.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.075
- Every single time a poop came up,

00:02:11.075 --> 00:02:11.908
I just laughed.

00:02:11.908 --> 00:02:13.896
'Cause there's nothing
more funny than poop.

00:02:13.896 --> 00:02:15.928
Something happened.

00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:17.832
He's got like four poops.

00:02:17.832 --> 00:02:19.585
I'm gonna clean up his poops right now.

00:02:19.585 --> 00:02:22.720
(beeping)
Oh, he's so much happier.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:23.788
- Randomly would mess--

00:02:23.788 --> 00:02:25.797
Would start pinging me if I was

00:02:25.797 --> 00:02:27.422
sitting there not doing anything,

00:02:27.422 --> 00:02:29.048
and be like, clean my poop, bitch.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.928
- It did not go as I expected.

00:02:30.928 --> 00:02:33.053
I lost my Tamagotchi.

00:02:33.053 --> 00:02:36.106
I'm super nervous because
I lost my Tamagotchi.

00:02:36.106 --> 00:02:38.649
I looked at home, I looked in my desk,

00:02:38.649 --> 00:02:40.065
but I can't find it anywhere.

00:02:40.065 --> 00:02:41.514
But I did my best.

00:02:41.514 --> 00:02:43.681
But, I did find it, right?

00:02:45.492 --> 00:02:47.059
It's just dead.
(descending toning)

00:02:47.059 --> 00:02:47.892
I just--

00:02:47.892 --> 00:02:50.037
Some people aren't meant
to parent things in life,

00:02:50.037 --> 00:02:51.035
and I realize that.

00:02:51.035 --> 00:02:53.671
- The only fight me and
Gotchi got in this week

00:02:53.671 --> 00:02:57.711
was when he woke me up at
7am just beggin' for food.

00:02:57.711 --> 00:02:58.756
Morning.

00:02:58.756 --> 00:03:01.078
My Tamagotchi won't stop beeping.

00:03:01.078 --> 00:03:02.727
It's so annoying.

00:03:02.727 --> 00:03:04.340
- Everyone wants to pick it
up and play with the buttons

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.349
and feed it and kind of relive

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:07.893
that joy they had when they were a kid.

00:03:07.893 --> 00:03:09.971
- You have a Tamagotchi!
- Yeah!

00:03:09.971 --> 00:03:11.829
It definitely brought back memories

00:03:11.829 --> 00:03:13.710
that I hadn't really thought about

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.231
since I moved here.

00:03:15.231 --> 00:03:17.344
- One guy actually next
to me on the subway,

00:03:17.344 --> 00:03:18.806
who heard the beep go off,

00:03:18.806 --> 00:03:20.687
and then turned to me and was like,

00:03:20.687 --> 00:03:23.474
whoa, that sound just brought me back

00:03:23.474 --> 00:03:24.971
straight to the 90s.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.084
- Even though the experience
wasn't as exciting

00:03:27.084 --> 00:03:28.570
as I expected,

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.659
I was happy to play like I
used to when I was a kid.

00:03:31.659 --> 00:03:33.156
These used to mean so much to me

00:03:33.156 --> 00:03:35.757
because they were kind
of my friends on the go,

00:03:35.757 --> 00:03:37.081
so it's just cool to think about that.

00:03:37.081 --> 00:03:38.996
- Bein' a Gotchi daddy was fun.

00:03:38.996 --> 00:03:41.214
Clearly, I'm not cut out to be a parent.

00:03:41.214 --> 00:03:44.139
- It made me miss being a
kid and just having fun,

00:03:44.139 --> 00:03:46.914
hanging out, and laughing about
cleaning up my Tamagotchi's

00:03:46.914 --> 00:03:50.048
poop really brought me
back to my roots, you know?

00:03:50.048 --> 00:03:51.975
(laughs) Put it on my
tombstone that I love

00:03:51.975 --> 00:03:53.978
to clean up Tamagotchi poop.

00:03:53.978 --> 00:03:55.301
It was so fun.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.551
(fast-paced pop music)

00:04:00.526 --> 00:04:02.830
(whirring and creaking)

